WEBVTT

00:00:01.730 --> 00:00:03.020
Excuse me.

00:00:03.020 --> 00:00:04.940
I'm looking for someone.

00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:06.560
What're they like?

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:10.110
He's small and thin,
with black hair and clothes.

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:11.940
What's his name?

00:00:11.950 --> 00:00:13.030
His name?

00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:16.370
He's named Richard.

00:00:17.240 --> 00:00:19.160
Does he live around here?

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:22.910
No, but I have faith that I'll meet him.

00:00:22.910 --> 00:00:24.330
The taste of blood.

00:00:24.330 --> 00:00:26.040
The scent of blood.

00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:27.670
That act must be the same.

00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:41.390
Richard, are you drunk?

00:00:41.390 --> 00:00:42.810
Yes.

00:00:42.810 --> 00:00:44.690
A little.

00:00:44.690 --> 00:00:46.980
Everyone's the same, anyway.

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:51.820
When they discover the real me,
they turn to flight.

00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:55.240
The field of battle is all I need.

00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:00.780
York of the white rose.

00:01:00.790 --> 00:01:03.370
Lancaster of the red rose.

00:01:03.370 --> 00:01:09.830
These royal houses with roses for
their crests battled for the throne.

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:14.630
People call their strife
the "Wars of the Roses."

00:02:51.940 --> 00:02:54.400
O God, God, God!

00:02:54.400 --> 00:03:00.240
Marrying that man was the start
of all my misfortunes!

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:03.910
I wish he would just stay missing.

00:03:03.910 --> 00:03:05.530
Edward.

00:03:05.530 --> 00:03:07.830
I'm joking, Mother.

00:03:07.830 --> 00:03:11.500
Our restoration would be
impossible without him.

00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:15.670
A Lancastrian revival will
restore your rights as well.

00:03:17.170 --> 00:03:20.670
But that man abandoned his son.

00:03:20.680 --> 00:03:26.810
A true king would never disinherit me,
his own flesh and blood.

00:03:28.390 --> 00:03:32.770
He did abandon me back then.

00:03:32.770 --> 00:03:35.520
Sobbing all the while

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:37.440
that he "couldn't help it."

00:03:40.610 --> 00:03:45.700
He is... no longer my father.

00:03:47.240 --> 00:03:51.660
In that case, Edward,
your mother commands you:

00:03:51.660 --> 00:03:54.710
- Retrieve His Majesty, King Henry.
- Why me?!

00:03:54.710 --> 00:03:59.590
It would be a fatal blow to us
if he fell into enemy hands.

00:03:59.590 --> 00:04:03.180
- But...
- If you insist that he is not your father,

00:04:03.180 --> 00:04:05.130
then prove it.

00:04:05.140 --> 00:04:10.350
Prove that unlike your father,
you can do your duty with distinction.

00:04:10.350 --> 00:04:15.480
Prove that you are the next King
of England, whatever he may be.

00:04:19.020 --> 00:04:20.150
Very well.

00:04:21.570 --> 00:04:27.580
I will bring him back for you,
and not for love of him.

00:04:29.540 --> 00:04:32.620
You're going hunting with Edward again?

00:04:32.620 --> 00:04:36.420
He's been infatuated with hunting
since that trip we took.

00:04:36.420 --> 00:04:38.750
Yes, quite "infatuated."

00:04:38.750 --> 00:04:40.000
I get it!

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:42.840
Edward wants to practice
in secret, doesn't he?

00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:44.680
Don't try to hide it.

00:04:44.680 --> 00:04:47.180
I merely accompany him.

00:04:47.180 --> 00:04:48.720
Lord Richard!

00:04:48.720 --> 00:04:50.970
A letter for Your Grace.

00:04:50.970 --> 00:04:53.140
Leave it in my room.

00:04:53.140 --> 00:04:56.140
Goodbye, George.

00:04:56.150 --> 00:04:58.980
Hey, is that a letter from Anne?

00:04:58.980 --> 00:05:03.240
And for you, Lord George,
another letter from Lady Isabelle.

00:05:03.240 --> 00:05:04.900
K-Keep your voice down!

00:05:04.900 --> 00:05:07.370
I merely accompany him...

00:05:10.620 --> 00:05:14.000
to preserve His Majesty's secret.

00:05:15.500 --> 00:05:17.830
I'm off to see Elizabeth.

00:05:17.830 --> 00:05:23.250
Spend a few days hunting and tell
anyone who asks that I was here.

00:05:23.260 --> 00:05:25.840
Is this really necessary?

00:05:25.840 --> 00:05:28.680
People will find out eventually.

00:05:28.680 --> 00:05:34.850
You're right. Our relationship will become
public knowledge sooner or later.

00:05:34.850 --> 00:05:39.810
And that's why I've decided to take action
before things get complicated.

00:05:41.480 --> 00:05:46.740
I'm going to marry her now,
while our secret is still safe.

00:05:46.740 --> 00:05:48.780
That doesn't sound like a jest.

00:05:48.780 --> 00:05:51.200
I never jest.

00:05:51.200 --> 00:05:53.450
You see, Richard,

00:05:53.450 --> 00:05:59.000
I doubt that I'll ever meet
another woman to match her.

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:03.670
If I let her go, I'll regret it
as long as I live.

00:06:03.670 --> 00:06:04.800
But still...

00:06:04.800 --> 00:06:09.010
You're already my accomplice.
Is that clear?

00:06:09.010 --> 00:06:13.720
Does love make people as blind as this?

00:06:16.770 --> 00:06:21.900
The king of a country,
marrying a minor noble's widow?

00:06:21.900 --> 00:06:25.110
Complications are inevitable.

00:06:25.110 --> 00:06:27.110
It's nonsense.

00:06:27.110 --> 00:06:31.820
He speaks as though
that woman is more valuable.

00:06:31.820 --> 00:06:37.290
As though she's worth more than
the crown that Father died for.

00:06:37.290 --> 00:06:42.630
Meeting you here delights me
more than any crown.

00:06:46.050 --> 00:06:48.720
This isn't that forest.

00:06:48.720 --> 00:06:50.380
He couldn't be here.

00:06:52.050 --> 00:06:54.760
That was our last meeting.

00:06:56.600 --> 00:06:58.850
I'll never see him again.

00:07:01.480 --> 00:07:03.690
He and I...

00:07:06.360 --> 00:07:08.280
should never meet again.

00:07:10.740 --> 00:07:11.990
Richard?

00:07:13.700 --> 00:07:16.330
Oh, I knew that God would unite us.

00:07:17.750 --> 00:07:20.460
I had faith that I would see you again.

00:07:20.460 --> 00:07:21.880
Have you been well?

00:07:23.080 --> 00:07:28.550
Why does he always turn up
in my path without warning?

00:07:30.720 --> 00:07:33.340
What are you doing here?

00:07:33.340 --> 00:07:35.930
I'd love to return
to that forest with you.

00:07:35.930 --> 00:07:39.180
You and I live in different places.

00:07:39.180 --> 00:07:41.270
Get back to your sheepfold.

00:07:45.310 --> 00:07:47.320
I'm not a shepherd.

00:07:48.570 --> 00:07:53.280
I'm a traveler now.
I've been traveling in search of you.

00:07:53.280 --> 00:07:56.830
You are my home to return to.

00:07:58.450 --> 00:08:02.920
Why are you so obsessed
with me, of all people?

00:08:02.920 --> 00:08:07.040
Because! Because you've been
my salvation all this time!

00:08:07.050 --> 00:08:11.050
I was your salvation? Me?

00:08:12.300 --> 00:08:16.600
You were my only solace
through all those days of war.

00:08:16.600 --> 00:08:21.140
So, please, let me stay with you.
It needn't be for long.

00:08:25.900 --> 00:08:27.860
Until the rain stops.

00:08:32.570 --> 00:08:35.360
Undress. I'll give you fresh clothes.

00:08:35.370 --> 00:08:37.530
Do you live alone?

00:08:37.530 --> 00:08:39.330
Do you want to know my past?

00:08:39.330 --> 00:08:42.540
No. I don't care what you are.

00:08:42.540 --> 00:08:45.290
It's you yourself that I like.

00:08:46.790 --> 00:08:52.130
You're lying. If you ever found
out about the real me...

00:09:00.810 --> 00:09:02.270
What?!

00:09:02.270 --> 00:09:04.480
You ought to undress too.

00:09:04.480 --> 00:09:06.690
I wouldn't want you to get sick.

00:09:09.110 --> 00:09:12.110
I'll bring you fresh clothes. Wait here.

00:09:13.320 --> 00:09:16.950
He may be womanish,
but he has a man's body.

00:09:18.030 --> 00:09:20.120
Of course he does.

00:09:20.120 --> 00:09:22.160
But I'm different.

00:09:22.160 --> 00:09:24.540
No matter how hard I train,

00:09:24.540 --> 00:09:26.750
my marks of womanhood remain.

00:09:28.170 --> 00:09:32.090
Binding my chest can't
fill the void within me.

00:09:37.550 --> 00:09:40.260
Hey! What are you doing in the kitchen?

00:09:40.260 --> 00:09:44.480
Making soup. I'd been hoping
to surprise you with it.

00:09:47.020 --> 00:09:49.020
Oh, wow! It's real food!

00:09:49.020 --> 00:09:51.770
Just so you know,
I've never cooked before either.

00:09:54.320 --> 00:09:56.860
Something's missing.

00:09:56.860 --> 00:09:59.910
How about cinnamon? I'll get some!

00:10:02.740 --> 00:10:07.660
Should a devout shepherd really
be dining this late at night?

00:10:07.660 --> 00:10:08.790
Well...

00:10:10.750 --> 00:10:13.920
I haven't eaten since yesterday.

00:10:13.920 --> 00:10:16.590
I'm sure God will understand.

00:10:16.590 --> 00:10:20.970
So this wasn't out of gratitude?
You were just hungry?

00:10:20.970 --> 00:10:23.720
No. I really did want to thank you.

00:10:23.720 --> 00:10:26.430
Don't worry about it. Just eat up.

00:10:26.430 --> 00:10:27.430
All right.

00:10:29.980 --> 00:10:31.520
It's delicious.

00:10:35.860 --> 00:10:38.490
I've never tasted such delectable soup.

00:10:38.490 --> 00:10:41.570
I'm sure farmers' soups
are nothing but beans.

00:10:41.570 --> 00:10:43.030
I don't mean that.

00:10:43.030 --> 00:10:46.040
Just that cooking for myself
tasted wonderful.

00:10:46.040 --> 00:10:48.370
I did most of the cooking, remember?

00:10:48.370 --> 00:10:51.040
Yes. That's what made it so delicious.

00:10:52.460 --> 00:10:54.630
Thank you, Richard.

00:10:57.260 --> 00:10:59.800
It looks like it will rain all night.

00:11:01.390 --> 00:11:03.100
I'll lend you a bed.

00:11:03.100 --> 00:11:04.300
You will?

00:11:04.300 --> 00:11:07.310
Our promise was until the rain stops.

00:11:07.310 --> 00:11:09.640
Just leave on your own in the morning.

00:11:10.770 --> 00:11:13.610
What am I saying?

00:11:13.610 --> 00:11:15.860
Can't we share a bed?

00:11:17.360 --> 00:11:19.240
Your room is that way.

00:11:19.240 --> 00:11:22.610
I want to keep talking with you.

00:11:22.620 --> 00:11:25.740
I can't bear to part with you
when I wake up.

00:11:25.740 --> 00:11:27.490
I'm not a child!

00:11:27.500 --> 00:11:29.250
Get to sleep on your own.

00:11:36.420 --> 00:11:39.170
I can't let this go on.

00:11:39.170 --> 00:11:41.340
If I spend any longer with him...

00:11:42.760 --> 00:11:46.180
Richard, what is your favorite thing?

00:11:48.020 --> 00:11:50.350
What's your favorite food?

00:11:50.350 --> 00:11:54.730
Your favorite song or color of sky?

00:11:54.730 --> 00:11:57.820
Your favorite game for rainy days?

00:11:57.820 --> 00:12:02.530
Don't confuse me any more
than you already have.

00:12:11.750 --> 00:12:14.000
It's really pouring.

00:12:14.000 --> 00:12:15.250
You sound pleased.

00:12:15.250 --> 00:12:19.340
I am! I'd love to go on talking with you.

00:12:19.340 --> 00:12:23.130
I'd rather not,
but a promise is a promise.

00:12:23.130 --> 00:12:27.180
Besides which, I doubt that Edward
will be back anytime soon.

00:12:29.680 --> 00:12:31.100
Strawberries.

00:12:31.100 --> 00:12:32.230
Huh?

00:12:32.230 --> 00:12:34.730
That's my favorite food.

00:12:34.730 --> 00:12:36.270
I love them too!

00:12:37.690 --> 00:12:39.270
Prince Edward!

00:12:39.270 --> 00:12:42.110
A man in the tavern claims
to have met King Henry.

00:12:42.110 --> 00:12:44.820
Are you sure he's not some lying drunk?

00:12:44.820 --> 00:12:48.990
He said King Henry was looking
for a man named Richard.

00:12:48.990 --> 00:12:50.450
Richard?

00:12:50.450 --> 00:12:52.830
You don't play cards or chess.

00:12:52.830 --> 00:12:56.750
How do you pass the time on days
you don't make sundials?

00:12:56.750 --> 00:12:59.040
I'm glad you remembered that.

00:12:59.040 --> 00:13:02.250
I'm not fond of competing
with other people.

00:13:02.260 --> 00:13:04.550
I want to hear more of your stories.

00:13:04.550 --> 00:13:06.840
I don't know any more.

00:13:06.840 --> 00:13:08.800
Even a fairy tale would do.

00:13:11.720 --> 00:13:14.770
I don't read as much as my brother.

00:13:17.480 --> 00:13:21.150
This is... the story of a demon child.

00:13:23.070 --> 00:13:29.030
On the day that child was born,
a terrible storm laid trees low.

00:13:29.030 --> 00:13:35.120
Crows croaked in the night to herald
the coming of an age of misfortune.

00:13:35.120 --> 00:13:38.670
The child's mother suffered
abnormal birthing pains

00:13:38.670 --> 00:13:41.920
and despised her hideous offspring.

00:13:41.920 --> 00:13:48.300
The prophets said that one day, everyone
would curse the day that child was born.

00:13:50.510 --> 00:13:53.390
Did no one love that child?

00:13:53.390 --> 00:13:55.680
Some approached him in ignorance,

00:13:55.680 --> 00:13:59.400
but even they left when they
learned he was a demon.

00:13:59.400 --> 00:14:03.480
Did anyone love that child?

00:14:03.480 --> 00:14:05.190
He was loved by...

00:14:12.580 --> 00:14:14.910
That wasn't a very good story.

00:14:14.910 --> 00:14:17.580
That's the end.

00:14:17.580 --> 00:14:19.500
Richard.

00:14:19.500 --> 00:14:20.710
Richard!

00:14:29.220 --> 00:14:31.680
Maybe I drank too much.

00:14:31.680 --> 00:14:34.430
I've never had so much wine before.

00:14:35.310 --> 00:14:41.560
I don't know why, but I always say
shameful things when I'm with you.

00:14:41.560 --> 00:14:45.020
Why do I only tell you?

00:14:45.030 --> 00:14:47.690
Because we're friends.

00:14:47.700 --> 00:14:50.700
Maybe with you, I...

00:14:57.000 --> 00:14:58.410
Richard.

00:15:01.040 --> 00:15:02.540
Please forgive me,

00:15:02.540 --> 00:15:03.790
O Lord!

00:15:05.550 --> 00:15:07.420
Oh, no!

00:15:07.420 --> 00:15:09.510
A-Are you all right?

00:15:09.510 --> 00:15:11.550
I-I'm sorry.

00:15:11.550 --> 00:15:14.720
I'm... not fond of lightning.

00:15:21.140 --> 00:15:23.360
I don't care for it much myself.

00:15:24.020 --> 00:15:27.280
I'll share your bed tonight.

00:15:28.780 --> 00:15:32.740
You called me your salvation.

00:15:32.740 --> 00:15:37.950
I think that I'm the one our meetings

00:15:37.950 --> 00:15:39.540
have been saving.

00:15:44.340 --> 00:15:48.750
If my father is in this area,
we haven't a moment to waste.

00:15:48.760 --> 00:15:50.300
I'll scout ahead.

00:15:50.300 --> 00:15:51.920
Please wait, Your Highness!

00:15:51.930 --> 00:15:55.550
We'll stand out if we all go.
You wait here.

00:15:58.470 --> 00:15:59.680
Henry?

00:16:02.060 --> 00:16:04.900
Could Richard be here?

00:16:06.190 --> 00:16:11.110
When I'm with you like this,
I could almost forget about England.

00:16:11.110 --> 00:16:12.860
You mustn't do that, my king.

00:16:15.410 --> 00:16:20.410
Tell me, Elizabeth, have you
ever heard this fairy tale?

00:16:21.750 --> 00:16:23.330
Somewhere or other,

00:16:23.330 --> 00:16:28.630
there lived a prosperous father who
owned a book that recorded the future.

00:16:28.630 --> 00:16:32.260
Even his son's fate was
written in that book.

00:16:35.010 --> 00:16:40.100
"He will marry the daughter of a poor
farmer who lives by the cathedral,"

00:16:40.100 --> 00:16:42.520
is what the book said.

00:16:48.020 --> 00:16:51.360
The father found that girl

00:16:51.360 --> 00:16:54.490
and tried again and again
to part her from his son.

00:16:56.320 --> 00:16:58.950
But every time, a miracle occurred...

00:17:00.750 --> 00:17:03.000
and brought the two together.

00:17:06.000 --> 00:17:11.130
The moral is that no one can defy fate.

00:17:21.180 --> 00:17:22.430
Richard!

00:17:24.060 --> 00:17:25.100
Hey!

00:17:25.100 --> 00:17:26.480
Are you hurt?!

00:17:26.480 --> 00:17:28.690
Damn it! What should I do?!

00:17:39.700 --> 00:17:41.700
Henry?

00:17:41.700 --> 00:17:42.910
Thank God!

00:17:44.620 --> 00:17:46.830
Did he...?

00:17:46.830 --> 00:17:48.170
Was I...?

00:17:52.380 --> 00:17:54.170
Look, Richard!

00:17:54.170 --> 00:17:57.800
It's a miracle! They weren't washed away!

00:17:57.800 --> 00:17:58.930
Look!

00:18:00.390 --> 00:18:02.310
Strawberries.

00:18:02.310 --> 00:18:04.930
They grow thickly on that bank.

00:18:04.930 --> 00:18:07.690
I'd hoped to make it a secret
and surprise you.

00:18:09.690 --> 00:18:12.860
You mean you didn't leave?

00:18:12.860 --> 00:18:14.400
Didn't I tell you?

00:18:15.610 --> 00:18:18.070
You're my home to return to.

00:18:27.620 --> 00:18:30.250
What did I just...?

00:18:30.250 --> 00:18:32.630
What am I thinking?

00:18:32.630 --> 00:18:36.170
Henry, you make me mad.

00:18:37.220 --> 00:18:40.300
I'm afraid I'm going to lose

00:18:40.300 --> 00:18:44.510
the answers I've gotten and...
everything else.

00:18:44.520 --> 00:18:46.430
But even so...

00:18:46.430 --> 00:18:50.480
Even so, forever and ever, I...

00:18:53.940 --> 00:18:55.650
We promised.

00:18:55.650 --> 00:18:58.610
Could we make another promise?

00:18:58.610 --> 00:19:01.030
If we could promise to meet again,

00:19:01.030 --> 00:19:04.700
I could live with that as
my home to return to.

00:19:04.700 --> 00:19:08.870
Don't. If I spend any more time with you...

00:19:08.870 --> 00:19:12.250
Please, Richard.

00:19:12.250 --> 00:19:14.340
The house's owner has returned.

00:19:14.340 --> 00:19:16.550
Don't come here again.

00:19:16.550 --> 00:19:20.130
I've never made a promise
to meet you before,

00:19:20.130 --> 00:19:22.890
but we still ended up like this.

00:19:22.890 --> 00:19:24.850
Yes, you're right.

00:19:24.850 --> 00:19:27.140
I'm sure we'll meet again.

00:19:42.700 --> 00:19:46.120
So you are a man, Richard.

00:19:46.120 --> 00:19:48.910
Tell me, what is she like?

00:19:48.910 --> 00:19:50.700
What do you mean?

00:19:50.710 --> 00:19:54.590
You don't need to hide it. Have you
arranged another rendezvous?

00:19:55.500 --> 00:19:57.130
No.

00:19:57.130 --> 00:19:58.630
Do you regret it?

00:20:01.220 --> 00:20:04.010
Not as much as your marriage.

00:20:04.010 --> 00:20:06.390
I don't regret that.

00:20:06.390 --> 00:20:09.220
I loved as my soul bid me.

00:20:09.220 --> 00:20:13.560
Our meeting was God's will.

00:20:13.560 --> 00:20:16.650
Look, Richard. It's beautiful.

00:20:24.620 --> 00:20:28.290
Edward seems in an awfully
good mood again today.

00:20:30.120 --> 00:20:33.370
Your Majesty, I wish to make a report.

00:20:33.370 --> 00:20:36.460
Warwick, you've returned.
Is your news good?

00:20:36.460 --> 00:20:37.790
Naturally.

00:20:37.800 --> 00:20:39.420
That's perfect.

00:20:39.420 --> 00:20:43.090
I wish to make an announcement
here today as well.

00:20:44.680 --> 00:20:47.970
After you, Earl of Warwick.

00:20:47.970 --> 00:20:49.470
Very well.

00:20:49.470 --> 00:20:54.100
Allow me to inform you all that an
engagement has been contracted

00:20:54.100 --> 00:20:59.400
between King Edward and Lady Bona,
sister-in-law to the King of France.

00:20:59.400 --> 00:21:01.480
Oh, what wonderful news!

00:21:01.480 --> 00:21:03.400
Congratulations, Your Majesty!

00:21:04.570 --> 00:21:06.370
Allow me to join in...

00:21:08.120 --> 00:21:09.120
Your Majesty?

00:21:11.290 --> 00:21:15.790
Warwick, ever since we vanquished
the Lancastrians in battle,

00:21:15.790 --> 00:21:20.500
a sturdy chain has bound
our souls together,

00:21:20.500 --> 00:21:22.460
has it not?

00:21:22.460 --> 00:21:23.920
As God is my witness.

00:21:23.920 --> 00:21:25.050
In that case...

00:21:25.050 --> 00:21:26.760
Don't tell me...

00:21:26.760 --> 00:21:29.720
I have something to tell you all as well.

00:21:41.650 --> 00:21:43.190
Allow me to introduce you.

00:21:44.610 --> 00:21:46.490
This is my wife.
